    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Released in 1989, The Seeds Of Love marked a bold evolution for Tears For Fears, expanding their polished synth-pop into richly layered rock, soul, jazz, and psychedelic pop. Built around the anthemic “Sowing the Seeds of Love,” the soulful “Woman in Chains,” and the elegant “Advice for the Young at Heart,” the album balances elaborate studio production with expressive vocals and ambitious songwriting. Its Beatlesque textures and expansive arrangements made it a striking departure from the band’s earlier new-wave sound, while its commercial success included a No. 1 debut in the UK and a Platinum certification within three weeks.\n\nThis 2LP edition presents the original album on special-effect blue vinyl, accompanied by a second disc of demos, B-sides, and rare versions that illuminate the songs’ development and the album’s creative scope. Several of these recordings appear on vinyl for the first time, making the set valuable to both longtime fans and collectors. Housed in a single sleeve with alternative artwork, it offers a distinctive presentation of one of Tears For Fears’ most musically adventurous and enduring records.",
